{"nodes": [{"id": "benchmarks_readme_benchmark_suite", "label": "actor-ts micro-benchmark suite", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "The numbers are comparative, not absolute: single-machine, single-JIT measurements are a lower bound on latency and an upper bound on throughput, useful for regression detection rather than marketing.", "source_file": "benchmarks/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "benchmarks_readme_run_all", "label": "run-all.ts discovery driver", "file_type": "code", "rationale": "Spawns every file in a subprocess and exits non-zero if any suite failed so it can gate CI, while still running every suite so one broken benchmark does not hide the rest; files prefixed with _ are helpers and skipped.", "source_file": "benchmarks/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "benchmarks_readme_harness", "label": "lib/harness.ts (runGroup, memoryGroup, runBenchmark)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "benchmarks/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "benchmarks_readme_smoke_mode", "label": "ACTOR_TS_BENCH_SMOKE smoke mode", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Collapses every case to a single unwarmed iteration; the numbers it prints are meaningless because one unwarmed sample measures the JIT, so the point is only to verify each suite still executes against the current src/ API.", "source_file": "benchmarks/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "benchmarks_readme_typecheck_bench", "label": "typecheck:bench (benchmarks-only compile)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The build tsconfig deliberately excludes benchmarks/, so a src/ change that orphans a benchmark used to be invisible; the typecheck is the stricter check because a missing barrel export is a compile error even when the binding is never called, whereas Bun elides an unused named import.", "source_file": "benchmarks/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "benchmarks_readme_highresnow", "label": "highResNow() runtime-neutral timer", "file_type": "code", "rationale": "Bun.nanoseconds() on Bun and performance.now() x 1e6 elsewhere, so most benchmark files run unchanged on every runtime.", "source_file": "benchmarks/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "benchmarks_readme_node_count_scaling", "label": "cluster/node-count-scaling.ts", "file_type": "code", "rationale": "Same sharded ask workload against 1/2/3/5-node clusters, each size in its own subprocess, to show the cost of cross-node shard forwarding.", "source_file": "benchmarks/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "benchmarks_readme_worker_count_scaling", "label": "worker/worker-count-scaling.ts", "file_type": "code", "rationale": "Bun Workers dispatching CPU-bound tasks round-robin - true multi-core parallelism, unlike a router pool inside one ActorSystem.", "source_file": "benchmarks/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "benchmarks_readme_router_pool", "label": "single-node/router-pool.ts", "file_type": "code", "rationale": "JS is single-threaded, so a round-robin pool gives in-flight concurrency for I/O-bound workloads, not CPU parallelism.", "source_file": "benchmarks/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "benchmarks_readme_snapshot_frequency", "label": "persistence/snapshot-frequency.ts", "file_type": "code", "rationale": "Write throughput and recovery time at four snapshot policies - the write-path/replay tradeoff on one page.", "source_file": "benchmarks/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "benchmarks_readme_rest_comparison", "label": "http/rest-comparison.ts", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "benchmarks/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "benchmarks_readme_benchmark_suite", "target": "benchmarks_readme_run_all", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_readme_benchmark_suite", "target": "benchmarks_readme_harness", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_readme_run_all", "target": "benchmarks_readme_harness", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_readme_benchmark_suite", "target": "benchmarks_readme_highresnow", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_readme_smoke_mode", "target": "benchmarks_readme_run_all", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_readme_typecheck_bench", "target": "benchmarks_readme_benchmark_suite", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "benchmarks/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "benchmarks_readme_node_co